---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Wills & estates"
  description="Wills, trusts, executor services and deceased estates in Centurion and Pretoria, from an attorney who has wound up estates for years."
  legal
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="M Jordaan Attorney · wills, trusts & estates"
    title="Make it easy for the people you leave behind"
    intro="A will is not paperwork. It decides who looks after your children, who gets the house, and how long your family waits for money."
  />
  <section>
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="gap:48px;align-items:start">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What I do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Wills, drafted and checked by an attorney, and safely stored</li>
          <li>Estate planning: estate duty, liquidity and trusts</li>
          <li>Executor services and the administration of deceased estates</li>
          <li>Help for families reporting a death to the Master</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Fees, on the table</h2>
        <p>
          Executor fees are set by law at up to 3.5% of the gross value of the estate, plus VAT. They are negotiable, and
          a reduced fee can be written into your will. Will drafting: <span class="tbc">fee coming soon</span>.
        </p>
        <h2>If someone has just died</h2>
        <p>
          Start with the <a href="/report-a-death">checklist for reporting a death</a>: the documents the Master's office
          asks for, in the order you'll need them. Or phone me, and I will sit down with the family.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="card-dark stack">
        <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--moss)">Free · two minutes</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:28px;color:#fff">How ready is your family?</h3>
        <p style="color:#C9D8CF">Ten plain questions grow a sunflower. Then see what the weather does to it.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/check" style="align-self:flex-start">Plant your sunflower</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
